    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-102548 has no real root because a real sixth root is nonnegative, making f(x) at most -3. Solving for the original input gives the inverses in q-7026, q-35217, and q-35310. Differentiation gives slopes 5, 2, and 2e+8 for q-101587, q-17247, and q-140431; q-11735 uses the exponential derivative 6^x\\ln 6. The means are 91/15≈6.1, 590/23≈25.7, 50/5=10, and 30/6=5. The specified means imply 36+2c=66 and 2+3b=50, so c=15 and b=16. For the circle questions, x²=1-y²; the depicted fourth and second quadrants select the positive and negative roots respectively. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
